{
 "slug": "deutschlandlied",
 "parts": {
  "orig": {
   "stanzas": [
    [
     "Deutschland, Deutschland über Alles,",
     "Über Alles in der Welt,",
     "Wenn es stets zu Schutz und Trutze",
     "Brüderlich zusammenhält.",
     "Von der Maas bis an die Memel,",
     "Von der Etsch bis an den Belt,",
     "Deutschland, Deutschland über Alles,",
     "Über Alles in der Welt!"
    ],
    [
     "Deutsche Frauen, Deutsche Treue,",
     "Deutscher Wein und Deutscher Sang",
     "Sollen in der Welt behalten",
     "Ihren alten schönen Klang,",
     "Uns zu edler That begeistern",
     "Unser ganzes Leben lang —",
     "Deutsche Frauen, Deutsche Treue,",
     "Deutscher Wein und Deutscher Sang!"
    ],
    [
     "Einigkeit und Recht und Freiheit",
     "Für das Deutsche Vaterland!",
     "Danach laßt uns alle streben",
     "Brüderlich mit Herz und Hand!",
     "Einigkeit und Recht und Freiheit",
     "Sind des Glückes Unterpfand —",
     "Blüh’ im Glanze dieses Glückes,",
     "Blühe Deutsches Vaterland!"
    ]
   ],
   "credit": "August Heinrich Hoffmann von Fallersleben (1841)",
   "url": "https://de.wikisource.org/wiki/Lied_der_Deutschen",
   "licence": "",
   "source": "de",
   "page": "Lied der Deutschen",
   "own": false,
   "also": []
  },
  "en": {
   "stanzas": [
    [
     "Germany, Germany above all,",
     "Above all in the world,",
     "When, for protection and defiance, it always",
     "Holds together like brothers.",
     "From the Meuse to the Memel,",
     "From the Adige to the Belt,",
     "Germany, Germany above all,",
     "Above all in the world!"
    ],
    [
     "German women, German loyalty,",
     "German wine and German song",
     "Shall keep in the world",
     "Their old, beautiful sound,",
     "Shall inspire us to noble deeds",
     "All our life long —",
     "German women, German loyalty,",
     "German wine and German song!"
    ],
    [
     "Unity and justice and freedom",
     "For the German fatherland!",
     "Let us all strive for that",
     "Like brothers, with heart and hand!",
     "Unity and justice and freedom",
     "Are the pledge of happiness —",
     "Bloom in the radiance of this happiness,",
     "Bloom, German fatherland!"
    ]
   ],
   "credit": "Translation: The Epoch Institute",
   "own": true
  }
 },
 "aligned": true,
 "tentative": false,
 "heads": null,
 "label": null,
 "lang": null,
 "scheme": null,
 "notes": [
  "line 1.1: 'über Alles' means 'above everything' (to be put before all else), not a claim to rule over other lands.",
  "line 1.3: 'zu Schutz und Trutze' is a fixed pair: for defence and for resistance (against attack).",
  "lines 1.5-1.6: Maas = the Meuse (river, west), Memel = the Neman (river, east), Etsch = the Adige (river, south), Belt = the Little Belt (strait, north, in Denmark).",
  "line 3.1: 'Recht' means both 'right' and 'law'; 'justice' is used here."
 ]
